            <ArticleTitle>[About wine intake and cardiovascular diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>845-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is a (almost) new current understanding of the health effects of alcohol consumption. The alcohol remains a risk factor in certain diseases. Recent population studies and plausible mechanisms suggest a protective effect of alcohol against coronary disease. International comparisons, starting from 1819, suggest that the type of beverage has a main role (the 'French Paradox').</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
